            {
              "id": "5deaa7dd-e6d7-3457-84d7-56041ad1022a",
              "name": "\"Dynamic Content in System Call Vulnerability: Use 'Subprocess' Module to Prevent Command Injection\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe code snippet provided is vulnerable to command injection. This is because it uses the `os.system()` function to execute a shell command that includes user-supplied input (`uploaded_file.temporary_file_path()`, `upload_dir_path`, `title`). If an attacker can control these inputs, they can inject arbitrary shell commands to be executed on the server.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should avoid using `os.system()` or any other function that executes shell commands with user-supplied input. Instead, use functions that execute commands directly, without going through the shell, and that allow you to pass arguments separately from the command itself.\n\nIn Python, the `subprocess` module provides such functions. Specifically, you can use `subprocess.run()` (or `subprocess.call()` in Python 2), passing the command and arguments as a list.\n\n## Source Code Fix\n\nHere's how you can rewrite the vulnerable code using `subprocess.run()`:\n\n```python\nimport subprocess\n\nsubprocess.run([\"mv\", uploaded_file.temporary_file_path(), f\"{upload_dir_path}/{title}\"], check=True)\n```\n\nIn this code, the command and arguments are passed as a list, so they are not subject to shell parsing. This means that even if an attacker controls `uploaded_file.temporary_file_path()`, `upload_dir_path`, or `title`, they cannot inject arbitrary shell commands.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following Python libraries:\n\n- `os`\n- `subprocess`\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP Command Injection](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Command_Injection)\n- [CWE-78: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an OS Command ('OS Command Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-78",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/78.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-78"
                ]
              }
