            {
              "id": "f4085cc7-4ff7-3814-9ded-e38188e7e80b",
              "name": "\"Access sanitized data by using form.cleaned_data[] over request.POST[] post form.is_valid() execution\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nIn Python, when handling form data, it's common to use `request.POST[]` to access the submitted data. However, this can lead to vulnerabilities if the data is not properly sanitized. This is because `request.POST[]` directly accesses the raw data that the user submitted, which could include malicious input.\n\nThe `form.cleaned_data[]` method, on the other hand, is used after the `form.is_valid()` method has been called. The `form.is_valid()` method checks the form's fields for any errors, including improper input. If the form is valid, the `form.cleaned_data[]` method can be used to safely access the sanitized data.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, always use `form.cleaned_data[]` to access form data after the form has been validated with `form.is_valid()`. This ensures that the data has been properly sanitized and is safe to use.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nInstead of:\n\n```python\nname = request.POST.get('name', False)\n```\n\nUse:\n\n```python\nif form.is_valid():\n    name = form.cleaned_data.get('name', False)\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the Django library to execute properly.\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-20: Improper Input Validation](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/20.html)"
              },
