            {
              "id": "9552c3dd-51c2-3ecb-97f4-1b4235797331",
              "name": "\"download_profile_pic\" function lacks rate-limiting, risking resource exhaustion.",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `download_profile_pic` function in the provided Python code is vulnerable to resource exhaustion attacks due to the lack of rate-limiting. This means that an attacker can make a large number of requests to download profile pictures, which can consume significant server resources and potentially lead to a denial of service (DoS) condition.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should implement rate-limiting on the `download_profile_pic` function. This can be done using various Python libraries such as Django Ratelimit, Slowapi, or Flask-Limiter for Django and Flask applications respectively. Rate-limiting will ensure that a user or IP address can only make a certain number of requests within a specific time period.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is an example of how you can implement rate-limiting using Django Ratelimit library:\n\n```python\nfrom django_ratelimit.decorators import ratelimit\n\n@ratelimit(key='ip', rate='10/m')  # Limit to 10 requests per minute per IP address\ndef download_profile_pic(request, user_id):\n    was_limited = getattr(request, 'limited', False)\n    if was_limited:\n        # Return a response indicating rate limit has been reached\n        return HttpResponse('Too many requests', status=429)\n\n    user = User.objects.get(pk=user_id)\n    filepath = user.userprofile.image\n    if len(filepath) > 1:\n        return redirect(filepath)\n    else:\n        return redirect('/static/taskManager/uploads/default.png')\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following Python libraries:\n\n- Django\n- Django Ratelimit\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html)"
              },
