            {
              "id": "c5d4254a-2e11-318f-ba16-d942543686f0",
              "name": "'Login' function lacks rate-limiting decorator, potentially causing resource starvation due to high traffic volume.",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe 'Login' function in the provided Python code lacks a rate-limiting decorator. This means that there is no limit to the number of requests that can be made to this function in a given time period. This can potentially lead to resource starvation due to high traffic volume, as an attacker could send a large number of requests in a short time, causing the server to become overwhelmed and potentially unresponsive.\n\nThis vulnerability is a type of Denial of Service (DoS) attack, where the aim is not to gain unauthorized access or data, but to make the service unavailable to legitimate users.\n\n## Mitigation\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, a rate-limiting decorator should be added to the 'Login' function. This will limit the number of requests that can be made to this function in a given time period, preventing an attacker from overwhelming the server with a high volume of requests.\n\n## Code Fix\n\nHere is a simple example of how you could add a rate-limiting decorator to the 'Login' function using the Django Ratelimit library:\n\n```python\nfrom django_ratelimit.decorators import ratelimit\n\n@ratelimit(key='ip', rate='10/m', block=True)\ndef login(request):\n    # existing code here\n```\n\nIn this example, the rate is set to 10 requests per minute per IP address. If this limit is exceeded, the decorator will automatically block further requests.\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThe provided code appears to be using the following libraries:\n\n- Django\n- Django Authentication (authenticate, auth_login)\n- Django Ratelimit (for the proposed fix)\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html)"
