              "id": "1010e26c-51f7-3790-be3a-a52daf0b115d",
              "name": "'profile_view' function lacks rate-limiting decorator, risking resource exhaustion with high traffic. Consider implementing rate limiting with 'django-ratelimit'.",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `profile_view` function in the provided Python code is vulnerable to resource exhaustion attacks due to the lack of rate limiting. This means that an attacker could potentially send a large number of requests to this endpoint, causing the server to consume excessive resources and potentially become unresponsive or slow down significantly. This type of attack is also known as a Denial of Service (DoS) attack.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, it is recommended to implement rate limiting on this endpoint. This can be done using the `django-ratelimit` library, which provides a decorator that can be used to limit the number of requests that a client can make to an endpoint within a certain time period.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is how you can modify the `profile_view` function to include rate limiting:\n\n```python\nfrom ratelimit.decorators import ratelimit\n\n@ratelimit(key='ip', rate='10/m')  # Adjust rate as needed\ndef profile_view(request, user_id):\n    try:\n        user = User.objects.get(pk=user_id)\n    except User.DoesNotExist:\n        return redirect(\"/taskManager/dashboard\")\n\n    if request.user.groups.filter(name='admin_g').exists():\n        role = \"Admin\"\n    elif request.user.groups.filter(name='project_managers').exists():\n        role = \"Project Manager\"\n    else:\n        role = \"Team Member\"\n\n    sorted_projects = Project.objects.filter(\n        users_assigned=request.user.id).order_by('title')\n\n    return render(request, 'taskManager/profile_view.html',\n                  {'user': user, 'role': role, 'project_list': sorted_projects})\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Django\n- django-ratelimit\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP - Denial of Service](https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/Denial_of_Service)\n- [CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-770",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-770"
                ]
              }
