            {
              "id": "a8cb9783-91ae-380f-aa38-7077d24ff0f8",
              "name": "'note_edit' function lacks rate-limiting, risking resource exhaustion from high traffic. Consider implementing 'django-ratelimit'.",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `note_edit` function in the provided Python code lacks rate-limiting. This means that it can be called an unlimited number of times in a given time period. This can lead to resource exhaustion if the function is called too frequently, as each call consumes server resources. This is a potential vulnerability as it can be exploited in a Denial of Service (DoS) attack, where an attacker intentionally sends a large number of requests to consume server resources and disrupt the service.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should implement rate-limiting on the `note_edit` function. This can be done using the `django-ratelimit` library, which provides a decorator that you can use to limit the number of times a function can be called in a given time period.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nFirst, install the `django-ratelimit` library by adding it to your project's requirements file or installing it directly using pip:\n\n```bash\npip install django-ratelimit\n```\n\nThen, import the `ratelimit` decorator in your view file and apply it to the `note_edit` function:\n\n```python\nfrom django.http import HttpResponse\nfrom ratelimit.decorators import ratelimit\n\n@ratelimit(key='ip', rate='10/m')\ndef note_edit(request, project_id, task_id, note_id):\n    # existing code here\n    was_limited = getattr(request, 'limited', False)\n    if was_limited:\n        return HttpResponse('Too many requests', status=429)\n```\n\nThis will limit the number of times the `note_edit` function can be called to 10 times per minute per IP address. If the limit is exceeded, a HTTP 429 'Too Many Requests' response will be returned.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- Django\n- django-ratelimit\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html)"
