            {
              "id": "aaecac06-e9b6-331e-b8ea-6e98ce1af7e8",
              "name": "'project_list' function lacks rate-limiting decorator, potentially causing resource exhaustion with high traffic.",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe `project_list` function in the provided Python code does not have a rate-limiting decorator. This means that there is no limit to the number of requests that can be made to this function in a given time period. In a high traffic scenario, this could potentially lead to resource exhaustion, as the server may not be able to handle the large number of requests. This could result in a Denial of Service (DoS) attack, where the server becomes unavailable to legitimate users.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, a rate-limiting decorator should be added to the `project_list` function. This will limit the number of requests that can be made to this function in a given time period, preventing resource exhaustion and potential DoS attacks.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a simple example of how you could add a rate-limiting decorator to the `project_list` function using Django Ratelimit library:\n\n```python\nfrom django_ratelimit.decorators import ratelimit\n\n@ratelimit(key='ip', rate='10/m')  # Adjust rate as needed\ndef project_list(request):\n    sorted_projects = Project.objects.filter(\n        users_assigned=request.user.id).order_by('title')\n    user_can_edit = request.user.has_perm('project_edit')\n    user_can_delete = request.user.has_perm('project_delete')\n    user_can_add = request.user.has_perm('project_add')\n    return render(request,\n                  'taskManager/project_list.html',\n                  {'project_list': sorted_projects,\n                   'user': request.user,\n                   'user_can_edit': user_can_edit,\n                   'user_can_delete': user_can_delete,\n                   'user_can_add': user_can_add})\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- Django\n- Django Ratelimit (for the rate-limiting decorator)\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html)"
