            {
              "id": "8dcc61c8-5749-3da8-b021-22c70e292a02",
              "name": "Use ITEM.user_id instead of ITEM.user.id to avoid additional query execution.",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nIn Python, especially when dealing with Django ORM (Object-Relational Mapping), using `ITEM.user.id` instead of `ITEM.user_id` can lead to an unnecessary database query. This is because `ITEM.user.id` first fetches the user object from the database and then accesses its id, while `ITEM.user_id` directly accesses the user id without fetching the user object. This can lead to performance issues and can also expose your application to potential security vulnerabilities such as SQL Injection.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this issue, you should always use `ITEM.user_id` when you only need to access the user id. This will avoid the unnecessary database query and improve the performance of your application. Also, always make sure to sanitize and validate any user input to prevent SQL Injection attacks.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nInstead of:\n\n```python\nusers_assigned=request.user.id).filter(\n```\n\nUse:\n\n```python\nusers_assigned=request.user_id).filter(\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies to execute properly:\n\n- Django\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP SQL Injection Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/SQL_Injection_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-89",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-89"
                ]
              }
