            {
              "id": "feb519b6-12d9-3041-9528-1f2d05df46d8",
              "name": "Prefer ITEM.user_id over ITEM.user.id to avoid additional query execution.",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nIn Python, when using Django ORM to interact with a database, the way you access related fields can have a significant impact on the number of queries executed. If you access a related field using the dot notation (e.g., `ITEM.user.id`), Django will execute an additional query to fetch the related object. This is known as a \"N+1 query problem\". It can lead to performance issues, especially when dealing with large amounts of data.\n\nIn the provided code example, `users_assigned=request.user.id` is used to filter `Task` objects. If `users_assigned` is a related field, using `request.user.id` instead of `request.user_id` will result in an additional query to fetch the `User` object associated with the `request`.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo avoid the additional query, you should use the `user_id` field directly. This field is automatically created by Django for ForeignKey relationships and contains the ID of the related object. By using this field, you can avoid the need to fetch the related object, thus reducing the number of queries executed.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is how you can fix the provided code example:\n\n```python\nmy_task_list = Task.objects.filter(users_assigned_id=request.user.id)\n```\n\nIn this version, `users_assigned_id` is used instead of `users_assigned`. This will avoid the additional query to fetch the `User` object.\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Django: A high-level Python Web framework that encourages rapid development and clean, pragmatic design.\n\n## OWASP Resources\n\n- [OWASP Code Review Guide](https://owasp.org/www-pdf-archive/OWASP_Code_Review_Guide_v2.pdf)\n- [OWASP Top 10 2017 Category A1 - Injection](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/2017/A1_2017-Injection)\n\n## Common Weakness Enumeration (CWE)\n\n- [CWE-89: Improper Neutralization of Special Elements used in an SQL Command ('SQL Injection')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html)\n- [CWE-564: SQL Injection: Hibernate](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/564.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-89",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/89.html"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-564",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/564.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-89",
                  "CWE-564"
                ]
              }
