            {
              "id": "d897366b-79fa-33d0-83fd-9f898c02e749",
              "name": "\"Search Function Lacks Rate-Limiting Decorator Vulnerability\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nThe \"Search Function Lacks Rate-Limiting Decorator Vulnerability\" in Python refers to a situation where a search function does not have a rate-limiting mechanism in place. This can lead to a Denial of Service (DoS) attack, where an attacker can send a large number of requests in a short period of time, causing the server to become overwhelmed and potentially crash.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate this vulnerability, you should implement a rate-limiting mechanism on the search function. This can be done using Django's built-in rate limiting or using third-party libraries such as Django Ratelimit. Rate limiting will ensure that a user can only make a certain number of requests within a specified time period.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nHere is a simple fix using Django Ratelimit library:\n\n```python\nfrom django_ratelimit.decorators import ratelimit\n\n@ratelimit(key='ip', rate='10/m')  # Adjust rate as needed\ndef search(request):\n    was_limited = getattr(request, 'limited', False)\n    if was_limited:\n        # Return a response indicating rate limit has been hit\n        return HttpResponse('Too many requests', status=429)\n\n    query = request.GET.get('q', '')\n\n    my_project_list = Project.objects.filter(\n        users_assigned=request.user.id).filter(\n            title__icontains=query).order_by('title')\n    my_task_list = Task.objects.filter(\n        users_assigned=request.user.id).filter(\n            title__icontains=query).order_by('title')\n    return render(request,\n                  'taskManager/search.html',\n                  {'q': query,\n                   'task_list': my_task_list,\n                   'project_list': my_project_list,\n                   'user': request.user})\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe code example requires the following library dependencies:\n\n- Django\n- Django Ratelimit\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-770: Allocation of Resources Without Limits or Throttling](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/770.html)"
